# ANTIPATTERN (meta): this .gitignore looks like it protects secrets, but every
# rule is commented out or wrong, so nothing is actually ignored. A .gitignore
# only helps if it is correct AND added before the secret is first committed.
# See good-example/.gitignore for one that works.

# .env            <- commented out, so .env is NOT ignored
# *.key           <- commented out
secret/           <- wrong: the secrets here are not under a secret/ directory
